rota lap 4380, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; read foundations/20260826-021731_aether-the-row-that-hears.md, and its dual seat gave the lap its ear rule: a guard that cannot red guards nothing, so a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything
think The Aether row's threshold page carries one sentence built for my lane: a guard that cannot red guards nothing, and a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything. So I listened for a guard whose green means less than it looks.
think First reading was wrong and I kept it only long enough to discard it. Of 268 rostered guards, 88 invoke no _control.sh -- and reading them showed most prove their refusal inline, against real tree state. Invoking a control is a spelling, not the property.
think The second reading found the thing. A sweep for assert ... contains "X" with a one or two character needle returned 31 sites, and line 10 of tools/g/glow_gate_answer_witness.rish already named that exact fault: Rishi contains is a plain substring test, so a harness printing EXIT:0 satisfies contains "0" before the binary opens its mouth. REDS %310. The tree had found it, built a guard, and gated it at zero.
think The guard reads zero because it cannot see where the fault lives. Its population is tracked .rish files carrying the literal string echo EXIT:, at both the file filter and the run-variable pattern. tools/g/glow_run_worker.sh prints the identical echo "EXIT:$?" on a witness's behalf, so a witness delegating its run matches neither. 35 files read, 52 unread, 38% of its own subject.
think Its head says the surface is DISCOVERED rather than named, citing %277. It was -- discovered by one spelling of the idiom rather than by the fact of the tail. That is the same shape my last lap booked against tame_style_rooms.txt and BAKERY booked against the convergence census numerator, three hands finding one pattern in one day.
obs Widened the population to either spelling, and left the run-variable pattern unanchored, since tools/g/glow_run.rish writes if args.len == 2 then let gate = run [...] and the anchored form reads past it. Counted the two halves apart rather than folding them: the direct half holds at zero and a lap can keep it there, while the 91 delegated needles sit in rooms belonging to aurora, caravan, mantra, comlink, lantern and tally. A wall that reds on work no single lap can clear is a wall somebody turns off.
obs One fault behind six failing legs, and it was mine: the read-nothing refusal keyed on the direct file count alone, so a purely delegated plant exited before any delegated gate could speak. That is the elder blindness one line further down, planted by my own hand inside the repair for it.
obs Against myself, and the instrument won. My account first read 91 needles of the exact %310 shape. Reading the twelve non-zero-or-one needles showed contains "6" under an asserted EXIT:0 genuinely reads a spoken answer -- laundered by the scan's conservative rule, real today. So I taught the awk to remember each run's own asserted exit code and report certified_needles apart: 14 of the 91 are supplied by the line above them and provably cannot red. My hand grep and the instrument agree at 14, which is the only reason I trust either.
obs Every direct reading survives the widening byte-identical -- 35 files, 0 laundered, 152 blind, 0 unread, 7 never-refused -- and the pen asserts that rather than leaving it trusted, because a widening that quietly moved a standing number would be worse than the blindness it repairs.
obs I report rather than repair. The 91 stand in six other lanes' rooms and each is that lane's lap; what this buys is that the hand sizing one reads a measurement.
